<section class="cs-section">
<div class="cs-section-label">
<span class="cs-section-label-text">Decision Log</span>
<div class="cs-section-label-line"></div>
<span class="cs-section-label-num">05</span>
</div>
<div class="cs-decision-list">
<div class="cs-decision-card">
<div class="cs-decision-header"><span class="cs-decision-num">01</span><div><div class="cs-decision-title">VB.NET over C#</div><div class="cs-decision-problem">Team proficiency and existing codebase alignment; Sanofi's internal standards favoured VB.NET.</div></div></div>
<div class="cs-decision-body"><div><div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-chosen">&#10003; Chosen</div><div class="cs-decision-col-text">VB.NET aligned with team expertise and Sanofi's enterprise standards for legacy .NET apps.</div></div><div><div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-tradeoff">&#9651; Trade-off</div><div class="cs-decision-col-text">C# would have provided access to a larger developer pool and modern language features.</div></div></div>
</div>
<div class="cs-decision-card">
<div class="cs-decision-header"><span class="cs-decision-num">02</span><div><div class="cs-decision-title">ASP.NET WebForms over MVC</div><div class="cs-decision-problem">Project built on .NET 2.0 in an era where MVC was still maturing.</div></div></div>
<div class="cs-decision-body"><div><div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-chosen">&#10003; Chosen</div><div class="cs-decision-col-text">WebForms provided rapid RAD development with server controls for data-heavy forms.</div></div><div><div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-tradeoff">&#9651; Trade-off</div><div class="cs-decision-col-text">MVC would have offered cleaner separation of concerns and better testability.</div></div></div>
</div>
<div class="cs-decision-card">
<div class="cs-decision-header"><span class="cs-decision-num">03</span><div><div class="cs-decision-title">Stored Procedures over ORM</div><div class="cs-decision-problem">Complex queries required centralized, DBA-managed data access.</div></div></div>
<div class="cs-decision-body"><div><div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-chosen">&#10003; Chosen</div><div class="cs-decision-col-text">All data access through SQL Server stored procedures for performance and security.</div></div><div><div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-tradeoff">&#9651; Trade-off</div><div class="cs-decision-col-text">ORM would have reduced boilerplate but lacked DBA control over query optimization.</div></div></div>
</div>
<div class="cs-decision-card">
<div class="cs-decision-header"><span class="cs-decision-num">04</span><div><div class="cs-decision-title">LDAP / AD Authentication</div><div class="cs-decision-problem">Zero sign-on friction needed for Sanofi employees.</div></div></div>
<div class="cs-decision-body"><div><div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-chosen">&#10003; Chosen</div><div class="cs-decision-col-text">LDAP integration eliminated separate user store and provided seamless SSO.</div></div><div><div class="cs-decision-col-label cs-tradeoff">&#9651; Trade-off</div><div class="cs-decision-col-text">Forms auth would have supported external users but added credential management overhead.</div></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
